<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Korean Liberation Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Korean Liberation Army was the armed force of the Provisional Government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">Republic of Korea</a>, founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chongqing">Chongqing</a> in September 1940 with Chinese Nationalist support. Its members fought alongside Chinese and British forces against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, including in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, and trained with the American OSS for a landing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> that Japan's surrender in 1945 made unnecessary. It is regarded as a forerunner of the South Korean army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/korean-liberation-army.jpg" alt="Korean Liberation Army" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Korean Liberation Army · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Korean_Liberation_Army.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
